WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.760
We're only a few months away from the return
of our favorite fast-talking, regenerating

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.200
degenerate Deadpool, and we finally got our
first look at Josh Brolin's Cable — and

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.460
all his tactical pouches — in the first
real trailer.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:15.459
Fortunately, there's plenty of other stuff
to dig into too.

00:00:15.459 --> 00:00:19.050
Follow along if you're unafraid of spoilers
as we break down everything you missed in

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.229
the Deadpool 2 trailer.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:22.460
Red eye

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.080
The trailer opens with our first look at Josh
Brolin's Cable, a.k.a. Nathan Summers.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:31.220
The character has been a beloved mainstay
of X-Men comics since his first adult appearance

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.550
in 1990, and his glowing eye is as much a
calling card for him as it is for his optic

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.870
blast-shooting father.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.420
Based on his ongoing narration about being
born in a war, we can surmise that the movie

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:47.180
will at least partially follow Summers' original
origin as the time-displaced son of Scott

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.600
Summers and Jean Grey's clone, raised in a
dystopian future.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.129
More machine than man

00:00:53.129 --> 00:00:57.410
In the comics, Cable is one of the most powerful
mutants in the multiverse, but his potential

00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:03.040
is dampened by the techno-organic virus given
to him as a child by the evil mutant Apocalypse.

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.700
The virus was meant to kill him, but he was
saved by a talking ship and a one-way trip

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.860
to the future, where he learned to keep the
constantly spreading techno-organic virus

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.890
confined to his left arm and eye — albeit
at the expense of the full strength of his

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.320
telekinetic powers.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.210
Whether Deadpool 2 will follow the convoluted
story is anyone's guess, but in recent iterations

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.189
Cable has used a tricked-out metal arm for
added combat effectiveness after being cured

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:28.740
of the original virus, so it could go either
way.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.800
Hope

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.799
Although the trailer didn't give away any
main plot points, the appearance of a battered

00:01:33.799 --> 00:01:38.031
teddy bear on Cable's hip has led to speculation
that one of the storylines Deadpool 2 may

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.399
be adapting is Cable's stewardship of Hope
Summers.

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:45.530
Unlike the rest of the Summers family, Hope
isn't actually related to Scott, even though

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.110
she bears a striking resemblance to Jean Grey.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:52.500
Instead, she was the first mutant born in
a world that had the mutant genome removed

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.299
by the Scarlet Witch's chaos magic power.

00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:58.840
Regardless, Hope Summers has been referenced
previously, when her name appeared in the

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.590
first teaser back in 2017.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.829
Up to 11

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:07.039
"What's the most pain you've ever felt?"

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:11.160
We're not sure who Cable's asking, but odds
are good that his gun is about to cause more

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.660
pain than the most they've ever felt.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.890
Cranking it to 11 is a great use of the immortal
gag from This Is Spinal Tap.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:24.620
"Why don't make 10 louder and make 10 be the
top number and make that a little louder."

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.520
"These go to 11."

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.260
But even better, it's a pretty perfect encapsulation
of Cable as a character and a concept.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.490
He's the most hardcore mutant in the world.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.740
Of course his dials go past 10.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.040
"Mutant freaks!

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.080
I'll show you how to stand up to…"

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.040
"Not today, friend."

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.600
Not a mustache

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:50.900
One of the best gags in the trailer is a snide
joke that makes fun of Warner Bros. digitally

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.580
erasing Henry Cavill's mustache for Justice
League.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.810
"It's a metal arm!

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.570
It's not like we're trying to remove a mustache!"

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:01.520
Based on what we saw of the mustache-less
Cavill in Justice League, a metal arm really

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:03.190
might be easier to make.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:07.910
That said, the best in-joke from the trailer
is still Deadpool mocking Josh Brolin's other

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.550
Marvel character, Thanos, and his quest for
the Infinity Stones.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.680
"I got the stones to help you.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.480
Noooo."

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.470
Domino

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.350
We also get our first look at Domino, played
by Zazie Beetz.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.900
This is the first time Domino has made it
to the big screen, although like Cable, she's

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.520
been a fan favorite for years.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:31.980
In the comics, she's a consistent member of
X-Force, the secret strike team of the X-family.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:36.670
She's an expert at shooting and stabbing,
but her best quality on any team is her mutant

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:41.450
ability, which encourages good luck around
her and means things usually tend to just

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.450
work out.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.830
We can expect Deadpool to make at least a
couple of jokes about her mutant power being

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.170
lazy writing, but he'd better hope she's on
his side.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:53.350
Another detail that the movie may or may not
address is that she also had a brief fling

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:57.400
with another character appearing in Deadpool
2: Colossus.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.480
Negasonic Teenage Warhead

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:04.000
One of the standout characters in the original
Deadpool was definitely Negasonic Teenage

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.000
Warhead.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.620
"That's the coolest name ever!"

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.040
It looks like she's back for the sequel.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.700
She's grown her hair out a bit, but looks
as punk and angsty as she was in the original,

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.410
so we should get some great interplay between
her and Wade Wilson.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:18.980
New team

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:23.300
In a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment, we see
Deadpool in a plane flanked by Domino, Terry

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.670
Crews, and two hard-to-see mutants.

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:29.220
It's possible that Crews could be playing
Bishop, the other time-traveling mutant on

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.760
the X-Men, but he's usually working against
Cable, and has rarely been on X-Force.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:37.860
"Don't make me hurt you."

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.770
It's more likely that he's playing either
Hammer or G.W.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:43.410
Bridge, both frequent Cable allies.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:47.730
Easier to spot is what looks like Shatterstar
standing between Deadpool and Crews.

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:51.970
In the comics, he's a gladiator from a future
dystopia called Mojoworld.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.960
In between Domino and Deadpool looks like
what could be Chamber, a mutant who drew the

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.470
short straw of mutant powers with a bio-energy
that constantly leaks from his lower face

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.120
and throat.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:04.710
Side characters

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.660
It isn't just mutants that are coming back
for the sequel.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:13.410
Blind Al, Vanessa, Weasel, and Dopinder are
all seen in the Deadpool 2 trailer, but we'll

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:17.160
have to see how much time they get onscreen
with such a packed cast.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:23.190
As far as Wade's unpowered supporting cast
goes, one character is decidedly absent: Bob,

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.760
the agent of HYDRA who was slyly referenced
in the original.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.220
"Bob?"

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:30.780
"Wade?"

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.950
We'll have to see if Disney's lawyers have
softened up enough to let Bob appear in Deadpool

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:35.950
2.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:36.950
Thanks for watching!

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.300
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.340
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

